    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d16-a1">

                <pb facs="0075" n="19" sameAs="frus:frus1876/pg19"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                    120.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Oblitas to Mr.
                            Reynolds.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Secretary-General of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">La
                                Paz, Bolivia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1876-05-04"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 4,
                        1876</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: By the political change which the people
                    and the army conjointly have brought about to-day, General Hilarion Daza has
                    been proclaimed provisional president of this republic, the office of
                    secretary-general of state having devolved upon me in person.</p>
                <p>To impart this knowledge to your excellency is my high honor.</p>
                <p>I subscribe myself, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. OBLITAS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>To the <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chargé d’affaires</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">of the Anglo-American Confederation</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
